{"id":"chatcmpl-954ac7bf-e9bf-4f3c-9494-af12e60c5893","object":"chat.completion","created":1795249328,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates a verification-first approach for medical image interpretation where laterality and anatomical orientation are critical. The strategy involves consulting a domain expert tool for initial interpretation, then explicitly verifying the proposed answer against known imaging conventions (e.g., lateral view laterality) before finalizing. The pattern emphasizes confirming spatial/anatomical claims rather than accepting a single model's output.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When interpreting medical images, always confirm anatomical laterality (left vs. right) against the imaging convention (e.g., lateral view orientation) before accepting a finding.\",\n    \"Use a domain-specific expert tool for initial interpretation, then route the proposed answer through an independent verification step to catch orientation or labeling errors.\",\n    \"For binary anatomical findings, explicitly state the spatial relationship (which side is higher/relative to a landmark) to disambiguate the answer.\",\n    \"Treat single-view or single-model claims as high-risk and require corroboration when the answer depends on orientation-dependent features.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical image interpretation\": \"Identify the imaging view and its laterality conventions first; use expert tools for findings, then verify orientation-dependent claims independently.\",\n    \"Binary anatomical classification\": \"Anchor the decision to a clear spatial landmark (e.g., relative height of hemidiaphragms, spine position) and confirm which side corresponds to the finding.\",\n    \"High-risk single-source answers\": \"Flag answers that rely on one view or one model as risky; add a verification call that specifically checks the failure mode (e.g., laterality confusion).\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the imaging view and its laterality convention (e.g., which side is which on a lateral film) before finalizing an anatomical answer.\",\n    \"Verify the proposed finding against an independent check that specifically targets orientation/laterality errors.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":465,"total_tokens":854,"completion_tokens":389,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":465},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":389}}}